.TH TITLE-EXTRACT 1 "September 2026" "Version 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
title-extract \- fast stream-oriented HTML title extractor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B title-extract
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.br
.B cat
\fIfile.html\fR |
.B title-extract
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B title-extract
reads HTML input from standard input or specified files and extracts the text within the first
.B <title>
tag. It parses tokens in a single-pass stream without building a DOM tree, achieving near-zero allocations and maximum execution speed.
.PP
Parsing terminates immediately when a valid title is extracted, or when the
.B </head>
or
.B <body>
tag is encountered.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Output version information and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. Title was found and printed to standard output.
.TP
.B 1
No title found.
.TP
.B 2
I/O error or malformed token stream.
.SH EXAMPLES
Extract title from a remote URL:
.IP
.nf
curl -sL https://example.com | title-extract
.fi
.PP
Extract titles from multiple local files:
.IP
.nf
title-extract page1.html page2.html
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Crafted for sovereign POSIX environments.
